# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 69 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, 2026-10-13, build 700bb9d; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 51.2 s to 4213.0 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 69 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, 2026-10-13, build 700bb9d; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 51.2 s to 4213.0 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 44
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.8
field_pull_wraps 78
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the first of two streams of 2026-10-13 from one relay launch, 69 minutes cut
# to what its video shows, captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with the mouse pointer in
# the picture and the frames a pointer move alone brings left out before the ring (those under
# a twentieth of the picture). The arrivals are the game's pairs: 99.9% of the batches in the
# 60 fps seconds are pairs, 0.28 ms apart at the median, and the 188 seconds in which a pointer
# moved in a menu kept their 60 pairs a second. The policy is the one the tree ships. The game
# hitched (20 to 100 ms) 302 times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more 56 times an hour, in
# 171 bursts, 40 of them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released 24
# times (21 an hour), 20 of them from 2071 s on. 13 come 0.2 to 0.4 s after a capture gap of 26 to 48 ms, 2 fall in or beside a menu (284 s,
# 2783 s), and 9 have no gap over 25 ms in the 3 s before them. A release lasts 22 presents at
# the median and 63 at the most. The worst blend run, 44 presents from 3285.6 s, is the release
# at 3285.7 s, 0.21 s after a gap of 40 ms. Of the 153 moves on the replay, 34 land more than
# 2 ms from a real frame.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 51.200 s, from the 2355
# marked frames in its first 39 s, which sit within 0.40 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 4184.0 s with no holes. Its first frame is gameplay; its last 22 s show a black screen (4214 s
# to 4216 s, out of the 60 fps regime), the inventory, a little gameplay and the pause menu, so
# the cut ends at 4213.0 s, 22.2 s before the video does. Every second inside the cut that falls
# out of the 60 fps regime is a hitch second, 17 of them in 17 runs, none longer than 1 s, so
# nothing was removed from the middle. The map, the inventory and loot screens are inside the
# cut and in the regime.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.8% against 0.8% (0.8% and worst run 44 on the dejitter arm, which is
# how the stream ran), worst run 44 against 44, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 77
# against 78. Counted over this window, blends are 2076 against 2045, repeats 617
# against 617, skips 163 against 162, pull wraps 79 against 79, and lock releases 24 against 24,
# each at the same moment. The replay makes 153 moves, 32 of them late, and the field's log has
# 152 in the window. The 31 blends, 1 skip and 1 move by which the two differ were not traced
# present by present.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 44
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.2
min_reseeds 65
max_pull_wraps 77
extra_lag_ms 75
